This looks like a stainless steel mixing bowl holding raw sliced vegetables: red onion, green pepper, red pepper, carrot, and what may be cabbage. The bowl seems to be about 25-30 cm across, and the vegetables form a thin layer covering only part of the bottom. I estimate the total at about 200 g.

Raw vegetables of this kind run roughly 30-40 kcal per 100 g, so 200 g comes to about 70 kcal. I don't see any oil or sauce, so nothing extra is added for that.

